      "answer": "$0.5\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Use constant-acceleration equations to express either $s_{AB}$ or $s_{BC}$ in terms of $a$ [M1]. $s_{AB}=2(4.5)-\\frac12a(2^2)=9-2a$ [A1]. $s_{BC}=2(4.5)+\\frac12a(2^2)=9+2a$ [A1]. $9-2a=\\frac45(9+2a)$ [M1; use the given distance ratio]. $a=0.5\\text{ m s}^{-2}$ [A1]. Alternative: any two relevant equations in $u,a,s_{AB},s_{AC}$ [M1], two correct [A1], three correct [A1], then use $BC=\\frac54AB$ to form a valid equation in $a$ [M1], giving $a=0.5$ [A1]. Alternative: $AC=4.5(4)$ [M1]; $BC=\\frac59AC$ or $AB=\\frac49AC$ [M1]; $BC=10$ or $AB=8$ [A1]; use $s=ut+\\frac12at^2$ on BC or $s=vt-\\frac12at^2$ on AB [M1]; $a=0.5$ [A1]. Total 5.",
